  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Malli Obuleshu vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 10 August, 2020 Author: K. Suresh Reddy Bench: K. Suresh Reddy The Hon'Ble Sri Justice K. Suresh Reddy Criminal Petition No.3082 Of 2020 Order:",
    "facts": "This is a Criminal Petition filed under Section 482 of the Code of Criminal Procedure seeking to quash the proceedings in FIR No.70 of 2020, dated 30.05.2020 on the file of B.Mattam Police Station, Kadapa District registered against the petitioners for the offence punishable under Sections 272, 273 & 328 IPC and Section 59(1) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (in short \"the Act\").",
    "arguments": "Counsel for the petitioners has places reliance on the common order dated 18.12.2019 passed by a coordinate Bench of this Court in Criminal Petition Nos.5421 of 2019 and batch, holding that \"tobacco\" does not fall within the definition of \"food\", as specified under Section 3(i)(j) of the Act, therefore, registration of FIR is not permissible.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Counsel for the petitioners has places reliance on the common order dated 18.12.2019 passed by a coordinate Bench of this Court in Criminal Petition Nos.5421 of 2019 and batch, holding that \"tobacco\" does not fall within the definition of \"food\", as specified under Section 3(i)(j) of the Act, therefore, registration of FIR is not permissible.",
